//! THE OBJECT-OP DISPATCH AND THE TRAP HANDLER (spec §3, §5.7).
//!
//! Handle-table lookup -> object type -> op table -> rights check -> op, and
//! then every op body the eight kinds have. It is the top of the kernel: an op
//! may reach any seam below it, and nothing below may reach an op.
//!
//! `ktrap` is the HAL's landing point for every trap taken from user mode, and
//! the frame it RETURNS is the whole of the context switch.

